.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rars-extract 1 "" rars
.SH NAME
rars\-extract \- Extract archive contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrars extract\fR [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-legacy\-name\-encoding\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-buffered\-decode\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-decode\-workers\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-dictionary\-size\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-member\-output\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-total\-output\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-reader\-workspace\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-header\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-header\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-scratch\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-scratch\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-filter\-memory\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-rar3\-vm\fR] [\fB\-\-overwrite\fR] [\fB\-\-in\-place\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-broken\fR] [\fB\-\-flatten\fR] [\fB\-\-ignore\-attributes\fR] [\fB\-\-symlinks\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Extract archive contents
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
Archive password (visible in process list \[u2014] prefer \-\-password\-file or the TTY prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads for parallel compression and extraction (default: all available cores)
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read password from file ("\-" for stdin); trailing newlines are stripped
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
Progress reporting mode for long\-running operations
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-legacy\-name\-encoding\fR \fI<ENCODING>\fR
Source encoding for legacy names without Unicode (e.g. cp850 or detect)
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-buffered\-decode\-limit\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum RAR 5 member size to decode in memory; larger ones stream (default 16m)
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-decode\-workers\fR \fI<N>\fR
Threads decoding RAR5/7 blocks ahead of the output; 0 decodes serially (default: up to 8)
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-dictionary\-size\-limit\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum declared RAR5/7 dictionary size (not total memory)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-member\-output\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum decoded output per logical member or archive comment
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-total\-output\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum decoded output per extraction/test call, or per archive comment
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-reader\-workspace\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum aggregate reader workspace per call (not process RAM)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-header\-count\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR
Maximum top\-level headers per physical archive parse
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-header\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum plaintext header bytes per physical archive parse
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-scratch\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Directory for RAR5 filtered decoding above the buffering threshold
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-scratch\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum temporary bytes for RAR5 scratch decoding
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-filter\-memory\-limit\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum workspace per RAR5 scratch filter
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-rar3\-vm\fR
Run RAR 3 VM filter programs other than the six standard ones. Off by default: they are arbitrary bytecode from the archive and can use a lot of CPU time. Enable only for archives you trust
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR \fI<OVERWRITE>\fR [default: never]
Behaviour when an extracted file already exists on disk
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
never
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
rename: Write beside an existing file as name(N).ext
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
Write each file at its destination instead of staging it; a failed member leaves a partial file
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-broken\fR
Keep a damaged member\*(Aqs file with what could be read of it, like unrar \-kb; implies \-\-in\-place
.TP
\fB\-\-flatten\fR
Write every file straight into the output directory under its base name, creating no directories
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-attributes\fR
Set no file or directory modes, like unrar \-ai: files are created 0666 and directories 0777, less the umask; times are still restored
.TP
\fB\-\-symlinks\fR \fI<SYMLINKS>\fR [default: inside]
Which symbolic links and junctions to make, like unrar \-ol, \-ola and \-ol\-; hard links and file copies are always made
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
inside: Only those whose target stays inside the output directory; the rest are skipped and reported
.IP \(bu 2
all: Every one as stored, wherever it leads; nothing is ever written through one
.IP \(bu 2
skip: None
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Archive (and optional sibling parts) followed by an output directory
